Question: Tìm $I=\int_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}}\frac{\cos x}{1+\tan x}dx$.
Answer: \[I = \int_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}} \frac{\cos x}{1 + \tan x} \, dx = 3\ln|1 - \tan \left(\frac{\pi}{4}\right)| + C\]

Sử dụng substitution \( u = \tan(x) \):

\[I = \int_0^\frac{\pi}{2} \frac{du}{(1 + u)^2} = 3\ln|\frac{1 - u}{1 + u}|_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{4}} + C = 3\ln\left(\frac{1 - \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}}{\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}}\right) + C = 3\ln\left(\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}\right) + C\]<|im_end|>
