Question: Cho\[\displaystyle I(R)=\iint\limits_{x^2+y^2 \le R^2}\left(\frac{1+2x^2}{1+x^4+6x^2y^2+y^4}-\frac{1+y^2}{2+x^4+y^4}\right) dx dy.\]Tìm\[\lim_{R \to \infty}I(R).\]
Answer: \[I(R) = \int_0^\infty \left( \frac{1 + 2x^2}{1 + x^4 + 6x^2 y^2 + y^4} - \frac{1 + y^2}{2 + x^4 + y^4} \right) dx dy \]

Sử dụng phân phối tích phân:

\[I(R) = \int_0^\infty \left[ (1 + 2x^2)(dx + 2xydy) - (1 + y^2)(dy + xydx) \right] \]

\[= \int_0^\infty \left( 2x^3 + 2xy^2 + 2y^3 - 2xy + y^2 \right) dx \]

\[= \int_0^\infty (2x^3 + 2y^3 - 2xy + y^2) dx \]

\[= \left[ \frac{x^4}{4} + \frac{y^5}{5} - \frac{y^3}{3} + \frac{y^2}{2} \right]_0^\infty \]

\[= \frac{\infty - 0 + 0 + 0}{4} = \frac{1}{4} \]

Vậy,

\[I(R) = \boxed{\frac{1}{4}}\]<|im_end|>
